  "body": "<!--\r\nPlease answer these questions before submitting your issue. Thanks!\r\nFor questions please use one of our forums: https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/Questions\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### What version of Go are you using (`go version`)?\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n$ go version\r\ngo version go1.16.4 windows/amd64\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n### Does this issue reproduce with the latest release?\r\nYes\r\n\r\n\r\n### What operating system and processor architecture are you using (`go env`)?\r\n\r\n<details><summary><code>go env</code> Output</summary><br><pre>\r\n$ go env\r\nset GO111MODULE=on\r\nset GOARCH=amd64\r\nset GOBIN=\r\nset GOCACHE=C:\\Users\\tdakkota\\AppData\\Local\\go-build\r\nset GOENV=C:\\Users\\tdakkota\\AppData\\Roaming\\go\\env\r\nset GOEXE=.exe\r\nset GOFLAGS=\r\nset GOHOSTARCH=amd64\r\nset GOHOSTOS=windows\r\nset GOINSECURE=\r\nset GOMODCACHE=C:\\Users\\tdakkota\\go\\pkg\\mod\r\nset GONOPROXY=\r\nset GONOSUMDB=\r\nset GOOS=windows\r\nset GOPATH=C:\\Users\\tdakkota\\go\r\nset GOPRIVATE=\r\nset GOPROXY=https://proxy.golang.org,direct\r\nset GOROOT=C:\\Go\r\nset GOSUMDB=sum.golang.org\r\nset GOTMPDIR=\r\nset GOTOOLDIR=C:\\Go\\pkg\\tool\\windows_amd64\r\nset GOVCS=\r\nset GOVERSION=go1.16.4\r\nset GCCGO=gccgo\r\nset AR=ar\r\nset CC=gcc\r\nset CXX=g++\r\nset CGO_ENABLED=1\r\nset GOMOD=C:\\Users\\tdakkota\\GolandProjects\\gh\\abc\\go.mod\r\nset CGO_CFLAGS=-g -O2\r\nset CGO_CPPFLAGS=\r\nset CGO_CXXFLAGS=-g -O2\r\nset CGO_FFLAGS=-g -O2\r\nset CGO_LDFLAGS=-g -O2\r\nset PKG_CONFIG=pkg-config\r\nset GOGCCFLAGS=-m64 -mthreads -fmessage-length=0\r\n</pre></details>\r\n\r\n### What did you do?\r\n\r\nhttps://go.godbolt.org/z/64qsjGTcd\r\n```go\r\npackage foo\r\n\r\nfunc foo(v uint64) (b [8]byte) {\r\n\tb[0] = byte(v)\r\n\tb[1] = byte(v >> 8)\r\n\tb[2] = byte(v >> 16)\r\n\tb[3] = byte(v >> 24)\r\n\tb[4] = byte(v >> 32)\r\n\tb[5] = byte(v >> 40)\r\n\tb[6] = byte(v >> 48)\r\n\tb[7] = byte(v >> 56)\r\n\treturn b\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### What did you expect to see?\r\nCompiler should generate \r\n\r\n```asm\r\n        MOVQ    \"\".v+8(SP), AX\r\n        MOVQ    AX, \"\".b+16(SP)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What did you see instead?\r\nCompiler generates \r\n```asm\r\n        MOVQ    $0, \"\".b+16(SP) // redundant zeroing\r\n        MOVQ    \"\".v+8(SP), AX\r\n        MOVQ    AX, \"\".b+16(SP)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAccording to SSA dump and rules, I see that one-byte shift-and-moves are folded to one `MOVQ` during `lower` pass, so zeroing cannot be elimated during `opt` passes. \r\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/blob/04cd717a269d94d3b3459a3aaf43bc71e3112b7a/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/gen/AMD64.rules#L1965-L1982",
